+// Mavergreen: the 10.9 runtime is the pkgs'. RuntimeVersions.def maps every released Swift
+// version to OS X 10.9, where the runtime is the swift-runtime pkg's; these four need 10.9's own
+// libobjc instead, which has none of them, so they read FUTURE, as a 10.9 target saw them before:
+// ObjCMetadataUpdateCallback (_objc_realizeClassFromSwift; it also keeps the legacy-layout path),
+// ObjCGetClassHook (objc_setHook_getClass), ObjCClassStubs (objc_loadClassref) and
+// ObjCIsUniquelyReferenced (objc_isUniquelyReferenced). Every feature: patches/compiler/0003-AUDIT.md.
+FEATURE(ObjCMetadataUpdateCallback,                     FUTURE)
+FEATURE(ObjCGetClassHook,                               FUTURE)
 
